{
  "_comment": [
    "Which pool rows are a drawn supplementary bout, shared by BOTH language",
    "implementations: drawnSupplementaryBout in internal/engine/competition.go",
    "(Go) and drawnSupplementaryBouts in web-mobile/js/admin_pools.jsx (JS, which",
    "reads the same rule from the wire fields). TestDrawnSupplementaryBout_SharedCases",
    "drives the Go side and the 'drawnSupplementaryBouts' block in",
    "web-mobile/js/__tests__/admin_pools.test.jsx the JS side. A change to the rule",
    "changes this table, and a copy that disagrees fails its own test.",
    "chusenCases is the second rule: a drawn representative bout whose two teams",
    "a recorded chusen has ranked is settled by the lots (daihyosenRuledByChusen",
    "in Go; the JS reads the ranked ids off the standings rows marked isOverridden).",
    "The lots must cover the bout's whole tied group: every team the pool's",
    "standings hold level on points with its two sides (standings lists the",
    "pool's rows as id and points; two sides no longer level are the group on",
    "their own, and a pool with no standings rules nothing) has to be ranked.",
    "stuck is what the Pools tab's notice names: drawn and not ruled by the lots."
  ],
